# Item_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Loot-driven genres (open_world_rpg, roguelite).

## 2. This document owns
- Item taxonomy: types, slots, rarity tiers, stack rules.
- Affix/mod system: pools, roll ranges, combination constraints.
- Drop tables (per source) and itemization curves.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Currency and consumable economy — Resource_And_Economy.
- Item names/flavor — Naming / Bible.
- Character growth granted by items — Progression.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Taxonomy / 2. Rarity & budget / 3. Affix system / 4. Drop tables / 5. Itemization curve / 6. Legendaries & uniques / 7. Crafting inputs (link) / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Item vs Resource: discrete loot objects vs flowing economy resources.
- Drop numbers are owned here; kill/loot *rules* belong to Gameplay.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every affix has a range and a target slot list.
- No drop table references a non-existent item ID.
